According to the [Source: Dignity and Respect Policy for Students] (3.3.1), harassment is any form of unwanted conduct related to any of the discriminatory grounds, which has the purpose or effect of violating a person's dignity and creating an intimidating, hostile, degrading, humiliating or offensive environment for the person. The nine discriminatory grounds upon which harassment is based are: 
1. Gender;
2. Family status;
3. Civil status;
4. Sexual orientation;
5. Religious belief;
6. Age;
7. Disability;
8. Race;
